## 3. Light Mode Color System

### 3.1 Neutral Palette (HSL)

#### Key Adjustments from Flip: Lightness = 100 - (Dark Mode Lightness), then manually adjust

| Token | HSL | OKLCH | Usage |
|-------|-----|-------|-------|
| `bg-darkest` | `hsl(0, 0%, 98%)` | `oklch(98% 0 0)` | Base background |
| `bg-dark` | `hsl(0, 0%, 100%)` | `oklch(100% 0 0)` | Card backgrounds (elevated) |
| `bg-mid` | `hsl(0, 0%, 95%)` | `oklch(96% 0 0)` | Hover states |
| `bg-light` | `hsl(0, 0%, 92%)` | `oklch(94% 0 0)` | Input backgrounds |
| `border-subtle` | `hsl(0, 0%, 90%)` | `oklch(92% 0 0)` | Dividers |
| `border-default` | `hsl(0, 0%, 78%)` | `oklch(82% 0 0)` | Input borders |
| `text-muted` | `hsl(0, 0%, 50%)` | `oklch(56% 0 0)` | Secondary text |
| `text-default` | `hsl(0, 0%, 25%)` | `oklch(35% 0 0)` | Body text |
| `text-emphasis` | `hsl(0, 0%, 10%)` | `oklch(20% 0 0)` | Headings |
| `highlight` | `hsl(0, 0%, 100%)` | `oklch(100% 0 0)` | Top border (white) |

**Key Adjustments from Flip:**

- Base background slightly off-white (98% not 100%)
- Cards are pure white (100%) to appear elevated
- Highlight is pure white for top-light effect
- Borders blend into surfaces

